legacy scalar blocked_by target together with a structured row asserting blocks on the same target is reported as its own finding code, separate from the cycle it causes; The remediation hint states the removal that breaks the cycle instead of advising that the finding be left as history debt; Validation or the mutation advisory refuses to introduce a scalar-and-row ordering contradiction on write, with a negative control proving the refusal fires; The eight surviving terminal cycles across 49 items are broken and the audit reports zero for the ordering-cycle code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"explainable-graph"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"A cycle finding names the specific stored rows whose removal breaks it, so the remediation is a command and not an investigation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Every audit finding that reports a symptom instead of a cause converts into a research task, and research tasks do not get scheduled. This is why eight cycles have survived every hygiene wave."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Makes the last remaining legacy audit code executable, and generalizes to any future ordering contradiction rather than only the historical batch."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"The finding reports the contradicting row pairs; a single documented removal per pair breaks every cycle; the same signature is detected on write so the class cannot recur silently."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"All eight surviving cycles were traced to one signature in a single scan this session, which the audit could have reported directly."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-96h7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-96h7","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:39:32.399Z","author":"harness:claude-code","sou